# Trivy ignore list — accepted / triaged vulnerabilities.
#
# Add a CVE ID on its own line ONLY after triage, with a comment explaining
# why it is accepted (not exploitable in our context) and/or a review date.
# Prefer fixing (rebuild image, bump dependency) over ignoring.
#
# The CI gate uses `--ignore-unfixed`, so vulnerabilities without an upstream
# fix do not need to be listed here; this file is for *fixable* findings we are
# consciously deferring.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-2026-XXXXX   # reason — owner — review-by YYYY-MM-DD
#
# Django 4.2.30 — GeoDjango remote code execution.
# Not reachable here: django.contrib.gis is not in INSTALLED_APPS, nothing imports it,
# and the database is plain PostgreSQL (no PostGIS / SpatiaLite backend). There is no
# 4.2.x fix because 4.2 LTS ended in April 2026; the real fix is Django 5.2 LTS.
# `exp:` makes Trivy stop honouring this line on that date, so the gate fails again
# instead of the deferral being forgotten.
CVE-2026-15307 exp:2026-12-31   # not reachable (no GeoDjango) — maintainer — review-by 2026-12-31
